\ A non-tail recursive helper defined inside a word body, called through that word. Every call
\ defines the helper again, so the file measures what a body-level definition costs per call in each
\ compile mode. On a release build the compiled helper runs slower than the interpreter in hybrid and
\ eager.

recursive-non-tail: ( n -- n ) [
  walk: stack-recursive ( n -- n ) [ dup 0 > [ 1 - walk 1 + ] when ] ;
  walk
] ;

20000 [ 3 recursive-non-tail drop ] times
